<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fridtjof Nansen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1861">1861</a>–<a href="/years/1930">1930</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fridtjof Nansen (1861–1930) was a Norwegian explorer, scientist and humanitarian. He made the first crossing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a> ice cap in 1888 and drifted across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arctic-ocean">Arctic Ocean</a> in the Fram in 1893–1896. As the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a>' High Commissioner for Refugees he organised the return of prisoners of war and famine relief and created the Nansen passport, winning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1922.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fridtjof-nansen.jpg" alt="Fridtjof Nansen" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry Van der Weyde · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fridtjof_Nansen_LOC_03377u-3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
